# Dimensions of faces on a drawing (an extension, roadmap 29.2): a
# circle extruded into a cylinder; its end face picked with the mouse,
# then dimensioned on the front view of the drawing by its diameter,
# from the Drawing Sheet screen, which stays as it is picked; then
# picked again and dimensioned by its length, which a face has none
# of, and a message says so.
key c
move 300 300
down L 300 300
up L 300 300
move 350 300
down L 350 300
up L 350 300
key esc
key x shift
move 285 315
down L 285 315
up L 285 315
menu View|Drawing Sheet...
tw
twmove 46 305
twdown L 46 305
twup L 46 305
edit front diameter
tw
move 285 315
down L 285 315
up L 285 315
twmove 46 325
twdown L 46 325
twup L 46 325
answer ok
edit front length
tw
save
